nodes.body:
@ispobock @xiezhq-hermann Could you review this bounded file-backend lookup fix and enable initial CI with `/tag-and-rerun-ci` if appropriate?

The registered CPU file suite passes locally (35 tests, including the new parent-failing regression). On a warm local filesystem, 32 component-path queries remain around 0.09 ms as the directory grows to 50k files, versus 22.11 ms for the parent scan; the PR includes the paired-run reproducer and limits the performance claim to this lookup path.

The current gate fails at **Require run-ci label**, before test execution. The author does not have initial CI-label permission. No additional GPU test tier is requested for this Python/filesystem-only change.

